 "function": "cloudgen.texture.regime_weights",
 "doc": "The mix generate() really passes: float64 latitudes and float32 back-traced latitudes (np.degrees of a float32 array is float32, the cold-air difference is then float64). Tolerance 1e-4 relative / 1.5e-5 absolute: the float32 degrees carry a 3e-6 deg rounding that the cold ramp (1.5/8 per deg) turns into ~1e-6 of weight; measured worst difference against an all-float64 evaluation 1.3e-6, tolerance about 10x. Outputs closed/open/street are the function result; convective (climate.convective_tendency of the latitude in degrees), cold (the cold-air ramp smoothstep(0, 8, |back lat| - |lat|) in degrees) and total_raw (closed + open + street before the normalization, which divides by it where it exceeds 1) are intermediates, there to localize a mismatch; they share the tolerance. params.constants holds the knees and weights written in the code.",
